cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the paper it accompanies, please cite them as below."
title: "Causal Attribution for Agentic Decisions: Estimators, Coupling, and a Traceability Specification"
abstract: >-
  Estimators for post-hoc causal attribution over LLM-agent trajectories, the
  coupling that keeps a direct effect estimable once contexts diverge, and a
  traceability specification read against Regulation (EU) 2024/1689. Includes a
  proof that the marginal total effect cannot separate an inert step from a
  decisive one, and a proof that the common-random-numbers total effect returns
  exactly zero for a decisive step on a measurable set of runs.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Ajay Pravin
    family-names: Mahale
    orcid: ""            # add once registered
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/designer-coderajay/p2-agentic-attribution"
keywords:
  - causal inference
  - mediation analysis
  - common random numbers
  - LLM agents
  - interpretability
  - AI governance
  - EU AI Act
  - reproducible research

